JO  - Microbiology Resource Announcements
PY  - 2020
AB  - We report the genome sequences of 10 Pseudomonas aeruginosa phages studied for their potential for formulation of a therapeutic cocktail; they represent the families Myoviridae, Podoviridae, and Siphoviridae. Genome sizes ranged from 43,299 to 88,728 nucleotides, with G+C contents of 52.1% to 62.2%. The genomes contained 68 to 168 coding sequences. © 2020 Farlow et al. This is an open-access article distributed under the terms of the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International license.
DO  - 10.1128/mra.00503-20
