PY  - 2025
AB  - Virus-like particles (VLPs) derived from bacteriophage MS2 are widely investigated for their potential as a vaccines and drug delivery platforms. We have previously demonstrated that MS2 VLPs can be modified by the insertion of an externally located peptide, resulting in the assembly of particles larger than those typically seen for the native form. Here, we show that these larger VLPs can be functionalized both externally and internally. Firstly, using SpyTag-SpyCatcher technology, we demonstrate external attachment of the trimeric RBD from SARS-CoV-2. Secondly, we demonstrate encapsulation of fluorescently labeled oligodeoxynucleotides or mRNA. Finally, we show that such decorated or loaded enlarged MS2 VLPs are efficiently taken up by mammalian immune cells.
