JO  - BIBE 2025 - Conference Proceedings, 8th International Conference on Biological Information and Biomedical Engineering
PY  - 2025
AB  - The proceedings contain 39 papers. The topics discussed include: docker-implemented program streamlines multiple GWAS analysis; integrating transcriptomics and epigenomics with co-attention for mild cognitive impairment progression prediction; an exploration of the association between BMI and inflammation factors based on gut micro biota data and mendelian randomization analysis; cross-modal multi-source transfer learning for predicting host species of bacteriophage receptor-binding proteins; the value of ultra-high-resolution susceptibility-weighted imaging minimum intensity projection in deep learning-based detection of cerebral microbleeds; an antibody mixing and coating method for consistently detecting clinical retinol binding protein 4 (RBP4); and FcBinder: a machine learning model for predicting antibody Fc segment binding peptides.
